  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">20 International and local lawyers moblised

Co-create strategies for Legal action on LGBTQ+ rights in Nigeria

Explore the creation of epistemic foundation of LGBTQ+ rights in African human rights jurisprudence.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LGBTQI+ persons in Nigeria</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Obodo legal residency program is an initiative to bring together national and international human rights and LGBTQ+ rights lawyers to discuss, deliberate, and strategise on legal approaches to LGBTQ+ rights advocacy in Nigeria. The residency will include legal and policy analysis, exploring strategic litigation approaches, legal programming approaches for grassroots engagement and empowerment, etc.</narrative>
  </description>
